 "n":"Highland haggis bon bons, mustard cream",
 "note":"Spiced lamb and oat balls crumbed and fried crunchy, mustard cream dip, Stephen wants seconds.",
 "how":"Spiced lamb and oat haggis rolled into balls, crumbed and fried crunchy, with a wholegrain mustard and cream dipping sauce. Fry 400g lamb mince with a diced onion, then add 80g toasted oats, 1 tsp pepper, half a tsp nutmeg and 150ml beef stock and cook until thick. Cool and roll into 20 balls. Roll in flour, beaten egg and breadcrumbs and fry at 175°C for 3 minutes until crisp. Simmer 150ml cream with 1 tbsp wholegrain mustard for 3 minutes for the dip.",
